            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0749" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/891: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-10">December 10,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>824. Department received today your telegrams 1906 and 1910 of December 8,
                    together with your undated telegram which contained Foreign Office note in
                    regard to existence of state of war between the United States and Japan.</p>
                <p>We hope that all goes well with you and your staff and other Americans in Japan.
                    Department has notified families of Embassy staff that you are all safe and
                    well.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
